# Every checkout gets the same bytes on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true converts to
# CRLF while a Linux one stays LF, so the same commit is two different
# trees. Two things here depend on that not happening: the shell
# assembly's name is a hash of the managed source it is compiled from,
# and tools/hot_reload_gate.ps1 matches source lines by pattern.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.crate binary
*.nupkg binary
